{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>A linen tunic, etc.</b> This tells that he does not minister inside in the eight garments in which he ministers outside, for they contain gold — because a prosecutor cannot become a defender — but in four, like an ordinary priest — and all of linen (Rosh HaShanah 26)." "<b>Holy garments he shall put on.</b> That they should be of the Temple's property (Sifra)." "<b>He shall wrap.</b> As the Targum renders: יָחֵת בְּרֵישֵׁהּ — 'he places on his head,' like ״וַתַּנַּח בִּגְדוֹ״ (Genesis 39) — and וַאֲחִתְּתֵהּ, 'and he wraps it.'" "<b>And he shall wash in water.</b> That day requires immersion for every change of garments. And he would change five times — from the inner service to the outer service, and from outer to inner — shifting from golden garments to white and from white to golden; and for every change, immersion is required, plus two sanctifications of hands and feet from the basin (Yoma 31)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:44.193982557Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}